                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "22085107",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198049877654",
                            "num_reviews": 14,
                            "playtime_forever": 132,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 100,
                            "last_played": 1460310489
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I cannot recommend this game. It is the first game for quite some time I regret buying...\n\nPro:\n- Some Graphics, due to Unreal 4 middleware/engine\n- Cool fireworks at the beginning\n\nKind of neutral:\n- Not complete, only 3 levels available, and in-game announcements for 3 more levels\n- It is a \"collection\" of non-entangled mini-games/levels\n\nContra:\n- Very bad english translation\n- Bad programming, eg. missing or jumpy animations ... if any \n- Ugly level design, badly aligned walls, big squared blocks as buttons...\n- In game advertisement for portugese youtuber/podcaster?? Very good for the mood...\n\nOne Level is quite adventurous, i liked it (Black Hole), the Dark Room level is just plain jump scare stuff in one room, hence the name, and the hospital level is a joke. It is so complicated still uninteresting to play. I made an animated png with the desciption how to play it :)\n\nhttps://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/133541/playing%20manual.png\n\nMaybe the game gets better over time, but I cannot imagine installing it again in the future. Sorry, there are other very good indy horror games out there...\n\n\n",
